Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: ga36mb-jd9366: experiment E4, slower DSI link

Experiment kernel of device-fixes 6.3 (D12, P-95 E4), never in the default image.

The default mode asks for 30 MHz; with pll-video locked at 297 MHz by the DSI
block, pll-mipi can only give 297 x 6 / 5 = 356.4 MHz, so the pixel clock is
29.7 MHz and each of the two lanes runs at 356.4 Mbit/s. This variant asks for
27.5 MHz: pll-mipi 297 x 10 / 9 = 330 MHz exactly, lanes at 330 Mbit/s (-7.4%),
same totals (1040 x 518), 51.05 Hz. If the hot fault is a timing margin of the
link, it should start later or not at all.
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-ga36mb-jd9366.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-ga36mb-jd9366.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-ga36mb-jd9366.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-ga36mb-jd9366.c
@@ -194,8 +194,13 @@
  * vsync 6. In the Allwinner counting hbp/vbp include the sync, so the back porch is
  * hbp - hsync and the front porch is the rest.
  */
+/*
+ * Experiment E4 slow link (device-fixes 6.3): 27.5 MHz is pll-mipi 297 MHz x 10 / 9
+ * = 330 MHz divided by 12 (24 bits over 2 lanes): lanes at 330 Mbit/s instead of
+ * 356.4, same totals, 27500000 / (1040 x 518) = 51.05 Hz.
+ */
 static const struct drm_display_mode jd9366_mode = {
-	.clock = 30000,
+	.clock = 27500,
 	.hdisplay = 640,
 	.hsync_start = 640 + 280,
 	.hsync_end = 640 + 280 + 40,
@@ -450,6 +455,7 @@
 	dsi->mode_flags = MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO | MIPI_DSI_MODE_VIDEO_BURST |
 			  MIPI_DSI_MODE_LPM | MIPI_DSI_CLOCK_NON_CONTINUOUS;
 	ctx->panel.prepare_prev_first = true;
+	dev_info(dev, "experiment kernel e4-slow: 27.5 MHz pixel clock, DSI lanes at 330 Mbit/s\n");
 
 	ret = jd9366_check_bus(ctx, dsi);
 	if (ret < 0) {
